From: steamac <steamac@fxgam.es>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 11:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: clamp expanded compressed-copy extents to the mip edge

STEAMAC-5E/5F crash in the buffer-to-texture leg of CmdCopyImage2.
The event does not retain its formats, so this is not proof of the
reported input, but a valid RG32_UINT -> 1x1 BC1 copy reproduces a
Metal validation abort at the same encoder entry point on M1 Max:
(destinationOrigin.x + sourceSize.width)(4) must be <= width(1).

Block expansion must stop at the destination mip edge, including
sub-block mip tails. Clamp all dimensions after format conversion.
The sentry-image-copy compressed suite round-trips 1/2/4/8 BC1
shapes byte-for-byte with Metal API validation after this change.

---
diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_copy.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_copy.c
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_copy.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_cmd_copy.c
@@ -214,11 +214,16 @@
       dst_size.z *= util_format_get_blockdepth(dst_format);
    }
 
-   /* After adjusting for compression, sanitize destination extents for 1D/2D */
-   if (dst_plane->layout.height_px == 1)
-      dst_size.y = 1;
-   if (dst_plane->layout.depth_px == 1)
-      dst_size.z = 1;
+   /* A block copied to a compressed mip tail can cover fewer texels than
+    * the block dimensions. Vulkan permits that edge copy; Metal requires
+    * sourceSize to stop at the destination mip's edge, not at the padded
+    * block boundary (e.g. one RG32 texel -> a 1x1 BC1 mip).
+    */
+   const VkExtent3D dst_extent =
+      vk_image_mip_level_extent(&dst->vk, region->dstSubresource.mipLevel);
+   dst_size.x = MIN2(dst_size.x, dst_extent.width - region->dstOffset.x);
+   dst_size.y = MIN2(dst_size.y, dst_extent.height - region->dstOffset.y);
+   dst_size.z = MIN2(dst_size.z, dst_extent.depth - region->dstOffset.z);
 
    struct mtl_origin src_origin =
       vk_offset_3d_to_mtl_origin(&region->srcOffset);
-- 
2.50.1
